Found during k91 (worker). Test helpers in test/*.test.ts (makeRepo, bare-repo setup, git wrappers) spawn git with {...process.env}. `npm test` started from a git hook (GIT_DIR/GIT_WORK_TREE exported) would build fixtures in that hook's repository – the k91 bug class on the test side. Fix: one test helper that spawns git through src/gitenv.ts gitEnv() (or strips the same list), used by every fixture; optionally have the test runner delete the repo-local vars at startup. Also: the k91 guard test compares with the installed git's `rev-parse --local-env-vars`; a CI git upgrade that grows the list turns it red on purpose – note that in the test.

